# MASTER PROMPT: JAPANESE CLUB — ADMIN CONTROL CENTER & JLPT STUDENT REGISTRATION PORTAL

## PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Extend the existing Japanese Club website by building a complete, secure, scalable, role-based club management platform.

This is a critical part of the project.

The system must support:
1. Faculty Member Management.
2. Admin Registration and Faculty Approval.
3. Secure Multi-Admin Control Center.
4. Student JLPT Registration Portal.
5. Student Registration Management.
6. Interactive Japanese Learning Lab.
7. Event Registration and Digital Check-in.
8. Anime and Manga Discovery.

The system must be designed for a real college environment, with multiple faculty members, multiple administrators, and approximately 1,000 student registrations.

The website already has its own cinematic Japanese aesthetic, Mount Fuji imagery, anime-inspired visual identity, Japanese and English language support, and nine public pages.

Preserve the existing website design.

The management platform should use the same brand identity but have a clean, professional administrative interface.

IMPORTANT:
Do not treat this as a simple frontend demonstration. Implement real authentication, database persistence, authorization, registration workflows, and administrative functionality.

==================================================
01. SYSTEM ROLES AND PERMISSIONS
==================================================

Create three main access levels.

A. FACULTY / SUPER ADMIN

Faculty members have the highest authority.

They can:

- Log in using faculty credentials.
- View all administrator applications.
- Approve administrator registrations.
- Reject administrator registrations.
- Block administrator email addresses.
- Unblock previously blocked addresses.
- View admin registration history.
- View all registered administrators.
- Assign and modify admin roles.
- Suspend and reactivate admins.
- Enable or disable student JLPT registration.
- Open or close student registration.
- Set registration start and end dates.
- View all student registrations.
- Search and filter student records.
- Export student data to CSV or Excel.
- Manage registration settings.
- View total registration statistics.
- View system audit logs.
- Manage events and announcements.
- View all system activities.

Faculty members must have complete control over the system.

B. CLUB ADMINISTRATORS

Multiple administrators must be supported.

Every administrator has their own unique:
- Name.
- Email address.
- Mobile number.
- Password.
- Assigned role.
- Account status.

Administrators must have role-based permissions.

Suggested roles:

1. President.
2. Vice President.
3. Secretary.
4. Event Manager.
5. Technical Administrator.
6. Anime Group Moderator.
7. Learning Coordinator.
8. Gallery Manager.
9. General Administrator.

Allow faculty members to create custom roles and configure their permissions.

Administrators can only access features permitted by their assigned roles.

For example:

Event Manager:
- Create events.
- Edit events.
- Delete events if authorized.
- View registrations.
- Manage attendance.

Technical Administrator:
- Manage website content.
- Manage technical configurations.
- View technical logs.

Learning Coordinator:
- Manage Japanese learning content.
- Create quizzes.
- Manage learning resources.

Anime Group Moderator:
- Manage anime and manga recommendations.
- Moderate community submissions.

Secretary:
- Manage announcements.
- View club records.
- Manage meeting information.

President:
- Access designated club management functions.

IMPORTANT:
Do not automatically grant every administrator full system permissions.

Only faculty/super admins can approve new administrators or assign privileged permissions.

C. STUDENTS

Students can:

- Register for the JLPT-related student portal.
- Log in to their account.
- View their registration status.
- Update permitted personal details.
- View Japanese learning resources.
- Access learning quizzes.
- View eligible events.
- Register for events.
- View event registration history.
- Access their student dashboard.

Students must never access admin or faculty management pages.

