14. Manage individual student registrations.

REGISTRATION TOGGLE:

When faculty enables registration:

- The registration form becomes available.
- Students can submit new registrations.
- Registration status becomes OPEN.

When faculty disables registration:

- New submissions are blocked on the server.
- Students see a registration-closed page.
- Previously submitted records remain available.
- Faculty and authorized administrators can still access the records.

Display a clear message:

"JLPT student registration is currently closed. Please check the website for future announcements."

IMPORTANT:

The registration toggle must be controlled by the backend database.

Do not implement it as a frontend-only button.

The backend must reject submissions whenever registration is closed, even if someone tries to submit an old form or directly calls the API.

REGISTRATION CAPACITY:

Default capacity: 1,000 students.

Faculty must be able to change this number.

Prevent over-registration.

Use atomic database transactions or equivalent concurrency-safe logic so simultaneous registrations cannot exceed the configured capacity.

When capacity is reached:

- Automatically close registration or mark subsequent eligible applicants as waitlisted, according to faculty settings.
- Display a registration-full message.
- Notify faculty.

