18. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

This system handles student and administrator personal information.

Security is mandatory.

Implement:

1. Server-side authentication.
2. Server-side role-based authorization.
3. Secure password hashing using Argon2id or bcrypt.
4. Email verification.
5. Faculty MFA.
6. Secure password reset.
7. Session expiration.
8. Rate limiting.
9. Login attempt protection.
10. Input validation.
11. SQL injection prevention.
12. XSS protection.
13. CSRF protection where applicable.
14. Secure cookies.
15. HTTPS.
16. Audit logging.
17. Duplicate registration protection.
18. Account suspension.
19. Secure file uploads.
20. Protection against unauthorized API access.

Never store plaintext passwords.

Never expose student information through public APIs.

Never put secret keys in frontend source code.

Never rely on hidden URLs as access control.

Implement least-privilege access.

For sensitive operations such as blocking admins, changing roles, exporting personal data, or changing registration availability, record who performed the action and when.

Follow applicable Indian data protection requirements, including appropriate consent, privacy notices, data minimization, retention and deletion procedures.

